# Swallowed promise rejection: `.catch(() => {})` (or `.catch(e => {})`) — an
# empty rejection handler attached to a promise (jsts#33, CWE-390). It marks
# the rejection as "handled" so no unhandledRejection fires, while discarding
# the error completely: network failures, parse errors and thrown exceptions
# all vanish silently. This is the async twin of the empty `catch {}` block.
#
# Why a NEW rule (verified false-negative on mestjs slop.service.ts,
# 2026-09-26): `fetch(url).catch(() => {});` was detected by no existing rule.
# The empty-catch rule (KEUR-ERR-001) only covers `try/catch`, not the
# promise-chain `.catch()` form.
#
# HOW: match a `.catch(` call whose argument is an arrow function with an empty
# body — zero params `()` or a single param `x` / `(x)`, then `=>`, then `{}`
# (whitespace only, which is what skip_comments leaves for a comment-only
# body). A `.catch` handler that logs, rethrows or does anything real has a
# non-empty body and does not match.
#
# RE2-safe: `[^)]*` for the param list is a single bounded star scoped to the
# parens; `\s*` inside the braces is bounded; no backreferences, no nested
# unbounded quantifiers -> no catastrophic backtracking. WARN, not block.
#
# @see docs/research/javascript-typescript.md #33, MDN Using_promises#error_handling.
id: KEUR-SLOP-001
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 1
title: Swallowed promise rejection — empty .catch(() => {}) handler
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: warn
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .js .ts .jsx .tsx
  exclude_paths: node_modules/ dist/ build/ vendor/
patterns:
  # `.catch(` -> arrow fn with 0/1 param -> `=> {}` (whitespace-only body).
  - regex: (?s)\.catch\s*\(\s*(?:\(\s*[^)]*\)|[A-Za-z_$][\w$]*)\s*=>\s*\{\s*\}\s*\)
    message: "Empty .catch(() => {}) — the promise rejection is caught and silently swallowed (jsts#33, CWE-390). Handle the rejection (log/rethrow) or let it propagate. @see KEUR-SLOP-001"
confidence: 0.8
fix: "Give the rejection handler a real body: `.catch(e => logger.error(e))`, rethrow, or remove the empty `.catch` and `await` the promise inside a try/catch so the error propagates. Never attach an empty handler purely to silence unhandledRejection warnings."
